o not have a flush or a straight. The opponent checked the Flop and Turn but led out with a bet of 372 on the River. This line often represents a trap with a flush, a straight, or a value bet with a pair. Given the board texture, my Ace-high has very little showdown value, and the opponent's bet into a scary board suggests they have connected with it in some way.\n\nReason: The probability that the opponent has a Flush (any diamond), a Straight (any Jack), or a Pair (any 2, 5, 9, 10, Q) is high. My hand loses to all these combinations. The small bet size (372 into ~1000) looks like a value bet designed to get paid by a marginal hand, rather than a bluff trying to force a fold. Calling is -EV, and bluffing into a 4-flush board is dangerous. Folding is the safest and most prudent option to preserve chips for better spots.\n\nAnswer: -1"}
