ably have picked a better hand.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: The current board is King of Hearts, 8 of Diamonds, 9 of Hearts. You hold the King of Diamonds and 10 of Spades, giving you Top Pair with a 10 kicker. This is a very strong hand in heads-up play. Your opponent showed passivity by calling pre-flop and checking the flop, suggesting they likely do not have a premium hand, though they could be drawing. The board is "wet," meaning there are potential flush (Hearts) and straight draws available. Checking back allows your opponent to see a free card and potentially outdraw you.\n\nReason: Betting is the best play here to extract value from weaker pairs (like an 8 or 9) and to protect your hand against flush or straight draws. Since you are behind in the overall game standings and nearing the end (Hand 19/20), you should look to build the pot when you have a strong edge. A bet of 200 chips is a reasonable size to charge draws and get value without overcommitting.\n\nAnswer: 200'}
